From 7bdf59fa29be275f17c5ef3099d16541ae3741c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:02:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] math: MATH_CountPopulation returns 32 bits under the port

HGSS defines MATH_CountPopulation as u8 (lib/NitroSDK/src/math/MATH_pop.c:4,6)
but declares it as int in nitro/wm/wm_internal.h:155 and
vct/vct_audio_internal.h:155. On the ARM EABI a caller with the int prototype
reads the whole of r0: the callee only promises the low byte, and GCC leaves
the rest of the register as the last intermediate value, so the vendored SDK
test read 0x04080C11 for 0xF0F0F0F1 instead of 17 (the low byte is right).
MWCC happens to leave the register zero above the byte for this body, which is
why the DS build and the game work.

Under SDK_PORT_3DS the declaration and the definition return u32, so the same
byte value is zero-extended and every caller, whatever prototype it uses, sees
17. The MSL/Metrowerks build keeps the original two lines: gcc-10 -E -P of the
file without the macro is byte-identical.

Checked by the vendored test_nitro test_math case (MATH_CountPopulation
(0xF0F0F0F1) == 17), which failed before this patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/math/MATH_pop.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/math/MATH_pop.c b/src/math/MATH_pop.c
index 32aa11b..92b57d0 100644
--- a/src/math/MATH_pop.c
+++ b/src/math/MATH_pop.c
@@ -1,9 +1,24 @@
 #include <nitro/types.h>
 #include <nitro/code32.h>
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+/* SDK_PORT_3DS: return u32, not u8. The DS build keeps the byte return; on
+ * the ARM EABI the caller sees the low byte of r0 and whatever the callee
+ * left above it, and HGSS itself declares this function as `int` in
+ * nitro/wm/wm_internal.h:155 and vct/vct_audio_internal.h:155, so a caller
+ * with that prototype (the vendored SDK test among them) reads 0x4080C11
+ * for 0xF0F0F0F1 instead of 17. A 32-bit return zero-extends the same byte
+ * value, which is what every caller of this function actually wants. */
+u32 MATH_CountPopulation(u32 x);
+#else
 u8 MATH_CountPopulation(u32 x);
+#endif
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+u32 MATH_CountPopulation(u32 x) {
+#else
 u8 MATH_CountPopulation(u32 x) {
+#endif
     x -= (x >> 1) & 0x55555555;
     x = (x & 0x33333333) + ((x >> 2) & 0x33333333);
     x += x >> 4;
-- 
